## The shortest path to closing it

1. Add `--root <build>` to `damage_predict.py` (decode the build's `VehicleDamage` with the same
   `t1_current` path `damage_audit.py --build` already uses) so Done criterion 2 exists.
2. Then `Tools/scripts/bm_damage.py` can do the rest in one pass, all pieces already proven:
   copy the health module to `…/00_shared/modules/health/batmobile_health_medium.vmodc`, apply the
   `VehicleDamage` rows of `t10_damage_edits.json` plus the wheels rows in the per-vehicle
   `custom_land_global.vmodc`, repoint the `.epe` `damage` int to
   `hash_jenkins("editor/entities/jc_vehicles/00_shared/modules/health/batmobile_health_medium.vmodc")`,
   add the new module's `.toc` record, and stage `Builds/bm-003` from `bm-002`.
